# Brand colors

All visual chrome must use [`lib/core/brand_colors.dart`](lib/core/brand_colors.dart) / `ShadTheme` scheme tokens. No ad-hoc hex for icons, images, borders, shadows, fills, or chart accents.

| Role | Light | Dark |
|------|-------|------|
| Primary | `#0F766E` | `#2DD4BF` |
| Secondary | `#CCFBF1` | `#134E4A` |
| Border | `#B7C9C5` | `#3A5552` |
| Gain (numbers up) | `#15803D` | `#4ADE80` |
| Loss (numbers down) | `#DC2626` | `#F87171` |

## Rules

- Icons / images: `colorScheme.primary` (or secondary well behind them).
- Borders / dividers / inputs: `colorScheme.border` or `input`.
- Shadows: `BrandColors.shadowOf(context)` only.
- Positive/negative **data**: `BrandColors.gainOf` / `lossOf` — never primary for P&L.
- CTAs / focus: primary; soft selected states: secondary.

```dart
// ❌ BAD
color: const Color(0xFF16A34A)
boxShadow: [BoxShadow(color: Colors.black26, ...)]

// ✅ GOOD
color: BrandColors.gainOf(context)
boxShadow: [BoxShadow(color: BrandColors.shadowOf(context), ...)]
```
